Package: libomx-domain0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libs
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: C loader of an OpenMixer contract domain: the library
 libomx-domain reads a contract domain (the installed
 contract.d/<domain>/<domain>.json and its catalogs, which
 omx-contract-data and the owners' packages install) at program start-up: a
 word, a range, a sentence, looked up by function instead of compiled in. A
 missing or invalid domain is refused with a code of CONTRACT_CODES. It is a
 start-up library and is never called from an audio thread. It reads JSON
 with jansson.

Package: libomx-domain-dev
Architecture: any
Section: libdevel
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, libomx-domain0 (>= ${binary:Version}), libjansson-dev, pkgconf | pkg-config, ${misc:Depends}
Description: C loader of an OpenMixer contract domain: headers and ABI list
 Everything to build a program on libomx-domain: omxcontract/omx_domain.h,
 omxcontract/omx_contract_codes.h (the CONTRACT_CODES values the functions
 return), libomx-domain.pc, the list of the library's exports
 (/usr/share/omx-contract/abi/libomx-domain.abi) and the omx-domain command,
 which opens a domain and prints a word or a range. A consumer requires the
 library at a floor, the lowest release whose functions it calls.
